# Purpose

This document specifies every screen in the Aura Platform.

Each screen includes:

• Purpose
• Layout
• Components
• Navigation
• Data Sources
• States
• Animations
• Haptics
• Accessibility
• Acceptance Criteria

This document is the implementation blueprint for every SwiftUI screen.

---

==================================================
SCREEN 01
Home Dashboard
==================================================

Purpose

The Home Dashboard is the heart of Aura.

Users should immediately understand the current state of their home and complete the most common actions without navigating elsewhere.

---

Primary Goal

Answer one question:

"What do I want to do right now?"

---

Layout

Navigation Bar

↓

Greeting / Home Name

↓

Suggested Activity

↓

Current Room

↓

Favorite Devices

↓

Scenes

↓

Recent Activity

↓

Status Cards

---

Components

• Greeting Header
• Home Status Card
• Suggested Scene Card
• Favorites Grid
• Room Shortcut
• Recent Activity Timeline
• Device Status Indicators

---

Data Sources

Aura Core

↓

Room Manager

↓

Scene Engine

↓

Device Engine

↓

Diagnostics

---

Animations

Header fade-in

Cards slide upward

Status updates crossfade

Suggestions gently animate

---

Haptics

Light selection when tapping cards.

Medium feedback when launching a Scene.

---

Loading State

Skeleton cards

Animated placeholders

No spinner

---

Offline State

Previously cached information remains visible.

Offline badge displayed.

Retry button available.

---

Accessibility

VoiceOver support

Dynamic Type

Minimum touch target 44pt

Reduce Motion support

---

Acceptance Criteria

Dashboard loads in under 500ms.

Most common actions require two taps or fewer.

